WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.352
Vectorization means applying a calculation to an entire array rather than processing one element at a time in a Python

00:00:08.352 --> 00:00:11.962
loop. Suppose we have an array of monthly sales values.

00:00:11.962 --> 00:00:19.091
If we want to increase every value by five percent, we can multiply the whole array by one point zero five.

00:00:19.871 --> 00:00:27.543
The same idea works for subtraction, division, powers, comparisons, and many other operations.

00:00:27.543 --> 00:00:34.703
Vectorized code is usually more concise and often faster because NumPy performs the numerical work using optimized

00:00:34.703 --> 00:00:37.373
low-level routines.

00:00:37.373 --> 00:00:44.073
As you practice, try to ask yourself whether an operation can be expressed across the whole array instead of writing a

00:00:44.073 --> 00:00:46.003
manual loop.
